1
00:00:09,069 --> 00:00:11,380
Ash is just ash. Completely.

2
00:00:11,460 --> 00:00:15,701
And ash is the wood, the
fire, the air and the time,

3
00:00:15,781 --> 00:00:19,075
appearing as ash. How can both be true?

4
00:00:19,886 --> 00:00:22,673
I am John Tan, known as Thusness.

5
00:00:22,753 --> 00:00:26,944
These are my own notes, from my
own practice and contemplation.

6
00:00:27,749 --> 00:00:32,343
In Part 5, I asked what experience
is like when no layer is left.

7
00:00:32,423 --> 00:00:35,590
It is direct, without anything in between.

8
00:00:35,670 --> 00:00:38,620
The clarity is exactly the appearances.

9
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:43,946
In the seen, just the seen. The seen
is complete. Nothing stands behind it.

10
00:00:44,026 --> 00:00:45,852
Nothing needs to be added to it.

11
00:00:46,678 --> 00:00:51,055
But everything in this series has also
said the opposite, just as firmly.

12
00:00:51,135 --> 00:00:52,875
Whatever appears depends.

13
00:00:52,955 --> 00:00:55,620
The ringing needs the bell, the striking,

14
00:00:55,700 --> 00:00:58,636
the air, the ear and the attention.

15
00:00:58,716 --> 00:01:01,290
Take one away, and there is no tone.

16
00:01:02,101 --> 00:01:03,597
So how can both hold?

17
00:01:03,677 --> 00:01:08,488
If the seen is just the seen, complete,
how can it depend on anything?

18
00:01:08,568 --> 00:01:11,414
And if it depends, how can it be complete?

19
00:01:12,233 --> 00:01:15,812
Each half, held alone, is easily misheard.

20
00:01:16,642 --> 00:01:22,051
Hold only the completeness, and each
moment becomes an island. Sealed off.

21
00:01:22,131 --> 00:01:23,727
Owing nothing to anything.

22
00:01:24,556 --> 00:01:30,019
Hold only the dependence, and each moment
becomes a small link in a long chain.

23
00:01:30,099 --> 00:01:31,935
Or a knot in a vast web.

24
00:01:32,015 --> 00:01:33,769
Never whole in itself.

25
00:01:33,849 --> 00:01:36,817
Always waiting for the rest
of the world to finish it.

26
00:01:37,637 --> 00:01:39,921
Neither picture is what is actually met.

27
00:01:40,001 --> 00:01:41,823
What is met is both at once.

28
00:01:41,903 --> 00:01:45,890
The Zen master Dōgen had a
name for this. Total exertion.

29
00:01:46,702 --> 00:01:51,867
The words come from his great work,
the Shōbōgenzō. Exhausting completely.

30
00:01:51,947 --> 00:01:53,706
And total dynamic working.

31
00:01:54,517 --> 00:01:57,059
I want to be clear where the idea belongs.

32
00:01:57,139 --> 00:02:00,374
It is not a Dzogchen idea.
I do not find it there.

33
00:02:00,454 --> 00:02:04,654
Its classical home is the Chinese
Buddhism of the Huayan school,

34
00:02:04,734 --> 00:02:07,430
and Dōgen gave it its sharpest form.

35
00:02:07,519 --> 00:02:10,904
For me, it is one of the
most important tastes of all.

36
00:02:10,984 --> 00:02:14,246
And Dōgen is one of its
most important voices.

37
00:02:14,326 --> 00:02:17,743
So the next three parts go
to him, one image at a time.

38
00:02:18,558 --> 00:02:22,568
Put as simply as I can. Each
event spends itself completely.

39
00:02:22,648 --> 00:02:24,511
Nothing is held back behind it.

40
00:02:24,591 --> 00:02:26,984
Nothing outside is needed to complete it.

41
00:02:27,064 --> 00:02:29,946
Nothing is carried over
from it into the next.

42
00:02:30,026 --> 00:02:32,518
And no cosmos is packed inside it.

43
00:02:33,333 --> 00:02:36,120
And here is the point
that joins the two halves.

44
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:39,774
The completeness is not something
apart from the dependence.

45
00:02:39,854 --> 00:02:43,733
The event is complete as its
conditions, wholly at work.

46
00:02:44,558 --> 00:02:49,329
The ash lacks nothing. Not because
it stands free of wood and fire.

47
00:02:49,409 --> 00:02:52,196
But because the wood and
fire are fully there,

48
00:02:52,276 --> 00:02:54,872
as the ash, with nothing held back.

49
00:02:54,952 --> 00:02:57,019
In the seen, just the seen.

50
00:02:57,099 --> 00:02:59,958
And the seen is its conditions, appearing.

51
00:03:00,773 --> 00:03:05,013
Total exertion is also the
hardest taste to put into words.

52
00:03:05,093 --> 00:03:07,867
It is not first understood as an idea.

53
00:03:07,947 --> 00:03:13,818
It shows itself as a change in the texture
of ordinary experience, after anatta.

54
00:03:13,898 --> 00:03:18,791
And you find yourself living it, before
you can explain it. So I use images.

55
00:03:18,871 --> 00:03:23,442
They point at a taste. They are not
claims about what the universe is made of.

56
00:03:24,262 --> 00:03:27,756
But before the images, two
things must be made clear.

57
00:03:27,836 --> 00:03:32,149
Without them, everything that follows
is easily heard the wrong way.

58
00:03:32,965 --> 00:03:36,612
The first. Seamless in
working, not one Whole.

59
00:03:37,409 --> 00:03:40,331
Turn a key in a lock, and the door opens.

60
00:03:40,411 --> 00:03:44,163
In that opening, the
key, the lock, the hand,

61
00:03:44,243 --> 00:03:47,206
the turning and the door
work as one opening.

62
00:03:47,286 --> 00:03:52,089
With no seam between them. Nothing is
missing for it. And nothing works apart.

63
00:03:52,906 --> 00:03:54,593
But they are not one substance.

64
00:03:54,673 --> 00:03:56,712
Not parts of one great Whole.

65
00:03:56,792 --> 00:04:00,462
Not waves on a single substrate.
The key is still metal.

66
00:04:00,542 --> 00:04:02,310
The hand is still flesh.

67
00:04:02,390 --> 00:04:03,968
The lock is still a lock.

68
00:04:04,048 --> 00:04:07,246
They do not have to be the
same stuff to work seamlessly.

69
00:04:08,078 --> 00:04:12,591
They work seamlessly, conventionally,
because none of them has a nature of its

70
00:04:12,671 --> 00:04:14,565
own that would block the meeting.

71
00:04:15,419 --> 00:04:18,872
Things with natures of their
own could never meet like this.

72
00:04:18,952 --> 00:04:23,219
They would stay outside each other,
touching only at their surfaces.

73
00:04:23,299 --> 00:04:25,289
Or they would have to melt into one.

74
00:04:26,097 --> 00:04:28,354
Nāgārjuna puts it exactly.

75
00:04:28,434 --> 00:04:32,688
Whatever arises in dependence on
something is neither that thing,

76
00:04:32,768 --> 00:04:37,122
nor different from it. And so it
is neither cut off, nor permanent.

77
00:04:37,933 --> 00:04:40,489
All the necessary factors must line up.

78
00:04:40,569 --> 00:04:43,192
Take one away, and there is no opening.

79
00:04:43,272 --> 00:04:48,002
And in that opening, all of them are
wholly at work. That is total exertion.

80
00:04:48,082 --> 00:04:51,879
The opening, complete, with
nothing held back behind it.

81
00:04:52,697 --> 00:04:55,864
Nothing missing means nothing
missing for this opening.

82
00:04:55,944 --> 00:04:59,741
It does not mean the whole cosmos
has been gathered into the lock.

83
00:05:00,549 --> 00:05:02,181
And it runs both ways.

84
00:05:02,261 --> 00:05:04,572
A key is a key only with a lock.

85
00:05:04,652 --> 00:05:08,367
A door is a door only in
its opening and closing.

86
00:05:09,182 --> 00:05:11,738
Holism puts a Whole behind the parts.

87
00:05:11,818 --> 00:05:17,295
The door opens, it says, because a deeper
Whole expresses itself through them.

88
00:05:17,375 --> 00:05:20,325
The opposite habit makes
the parts the real stuff,

89
00:05:20,405 --> 00:05:23,735
and the opening a mere
name. Neither is found.

90
00:05:23,815 --> 00:05:26,032
There is just the opening, complete.

91
00:05:26,112 --> 00:05:29,147
And the factors, designated
together with it.

92
00:05:29,957 --> 00:05:34,564
So seamless working does not mean
wholeness, in the sense of holism.

93
00:05:34,644 --> 00:05:39,157
It is seamless because what appears
is empty of a nature of its own,

94
00:05:39,237 --> 00:05:44,691
and arises dependently with its
conditions. That is all. And it is enough.

95
00:05:45,526 --> 00:05:49,092
The second. Designated
together, without a given.

96
00:05:49,909 --> 00:05:53,647
I will say designated together
many times in these parts.

97
00:05:53,727 --> 00:05:55,390
And the phrase needs a guard.

98
00:05:56,214 --> 00:05:59,504
When I say the rower and the
boat are designated together,

99
00:05:59,584 --> 00:06:03,838
I do not mean two things already
there, with names stuck on afterwards.

100
00:06:03,918 --> 00:06:08,322
Nor do I mean one seamless stuff,
which names then cut into pieces.

101
00:06:08,402 --> 00:06:12,728
That would be the given again.
Either as many things, or as one.

102
00:06:13,533 --> 00:06:18,697
I mean that rower and boat stand out as
rower and boat only in the one rowing.

103
00:06:18,777 --> 00:06:20,984
The singling out is part of the appearing.

104
00:06:21,793 --> 00:06:27,270
It needs no words. The bee singles out
the flower, and a baby its mother's face,

105
00:06:27,350 --> 00:06:30,544
long before any name.
And it makes nothing.

106
00:06:30,624 --> 00:06:32,868
It is not a mind creating the world.

107
00:06:32,948 --> 00:06:35,318
And it is not words creating things.

108
00:06:36,125 --> 00:06:39,686
Nor does anyone stand outside,
doing the designating.

109
00:06:39,766 --> 00:06:43,151
The one who singles out is
singled out in the same event.

110
00:06:43,231 --> 00:06:45,243
As the seer is in the seen.

111
00:06:45,323 --> 00:06:47,095
And the seen in the seer.

112
00:06:47,899 --> 00:06:50,102
And the basis is not found either.

113
00:06:50,182 --> 00:06:54,463
Candrakīrti's chariot is designated
in dependence on its parts.

114
00:06:54,543 --> 00:06:58,308
But the parts are not a given
base. They are designated too.

115
00:06:58,388 --> 00:07:00,459
And no floor is ever reached.

116
00:07:01,261 --> 00:07:04,822
Nāgārjuna joins all of this in one verse.

117
00:07:04,902 --> 00:07:07,458
Dependent arising is emptiness.

118
00:07:07,538 --> 00:07:11,199
That is designation in dependence.
And that is the Middle Way.

119
00:07:12,030 --> 00:07:14,423
This is why Section 1 came first.

120
00:07:14,503 --> 00:07:17,045
While a given is still assumed underneath,

121
00:07:17,125 --> 00:07:20,823
designation can only be
heard as labels on raw stuff.

122
00:07:20,903 --> 00:07:26,733
Only once no finished world, no raw
data and no seamless substance is left

123
00:07:26,813 --> 00:07:30,447
underneath, can designation
be heard without one.

124
00:07:31,285 --> 00:07:32,691
Three ways of seeing.

125
00:07:33,817 --> 00:07:37,174
Each of Dōgen's images
can be seen three ways.

126
00:07:37,254 --> 00:07:39,964
And I find it helps to
see all three at once.

127
00:07:40,794 --> 00:07:44,804
The substantialist way. There are
things, standing on their own.

128
00:07:44,884 --> 00:07:47,920
And the event happens
between them, or to them.

129
00:07:48,742 --> 00:07:53,499
The way of anatta. The one standing
outside the event, the watcher,

130
00:07:53,579 --> 00:07:58,961
the doer, the seeker, is not found.
There is just the seeing. The rowing.

131
00:07:59,041 --> 00:08:00,241
The swimming.

132
00:08:00,794 --> 00:08:02,630
The way of dependent arising.

133
00:08:02,710 --> 00:08:06,149
What is left is not a bare
event, cut off from everything.

134
00:08:06,229 --> 00:08:10,361
It is complete as its conditions,
designated together with them.

135
00:08:10,441 --> 00:08:14,537
Here the taste of total
exertion is direct, and obvious.

136
00:08:15,366 --> 00:08:18,371
These are not three stages
that I have to climb,

137
00:08:18,451 --> 00:08:21,292
one after the other, by sudden insights.

138
00:08:21,372 --> 00:08:26,020
With a keen eye, all three show in
the same image, at the same time.

139
00:08:26,100 --> 00:08:31,459
And Dōgen's images are good precisely
because each one shows all three.

140
00:08:32,277 --> 00:08:33,601
So, which holds?

141
00:08:34,862 --> 00:08:39,796
By experience. When the door opens,
do I meet a key that opens it alone?

142
00:08:39,876 --> 00:08:42,500
Or a great Whole, opening
it through the key?

143
00:08:42,580 --> 00:08:44,905
What is met is the opening, complete.

144
00:08:44,985 --> 00:08:48,682
With the key, the hand and
the lock all at work in it.

145
00:08:48,762 --> 00:08:52,518
And at no point do I meet labels,
stuck on things already there.

146
00:08:53,346 --> 00:08:54,285
By logic.

147
00:08:54,365 --> 00:08:58,851
If the key had a nature of its own,
it would either stay outside the lock,

148
00:08:58,931 --> 00:09:01,962
or merge with it. It could
not simply work with it.

149
00:09:02,042 --> 00:09:06,568
If the opening were the same as the
key, the key alone would open the door.

150
00:09:06,648 --> 00:09:10,753
If it were wholly other than the
key, the door would open without one.

151
00:09:10,833 --> 00:09:13,062
Neither the same, nor different.

152
00:09:13,142 --> 00:09:16,758
And a Whole behind it all would
need its own parts to be a whole.

153
00:09:16,838 --> 00:09:18,869
It is no better off than the key.

154
00:09:19,702 --> 00:09:22,571
By working. Nothing
works the less for this.

155
00:09:22,651 --> 00:09:24,989
The key opens the door, every time.

156
00:09:25,069 --> 00:09:28,078
With no essence, and no Whole behind it.

157
00:09:28,885 --> 00:09:31,998
So the view of separate
things linked by conditions,

158
00:09:32,078 --> 00:09:37,079
or of one great Whole showing itself
in parts, is not the truer one.

159
00:09:37,159 --> 00:09:41,146
Both are the default, carried
by habit, and by nouns.

160
00:09:41,945 --> 00:09:47,191
None of this makes my everyday words
false. I turn the key. The door opens.

161
00:09:47,271 --> 00:09:52,915
What fails is only a key, a door,
or a cosmos, standing on its own.

162
00:09:53,733 --> 00:09:58,304
This is Section 2, Part 6 of
the Dependent Arising series.

163
00:09:59,113 --> 00:10:02,837
In Part 7, I take
Dōgen's first two images.

164
00:10:02,917 --> 00:10:07,131
The shore that seems to move,
where no seat is left outside.

165
00:10:07,211 --> 00:10:11,850
And the boat that carries its rower,
where no doer stands behind the act.

